From 02aae35fdc71b90535771b398588ebf8bb9600ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:43:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc: the radio readers are stopped before every path that
 tears the radios down

rpunctd arms a 4 s chanim_stats window on every Dynamic radio each tick,
reaper_bwfloor reads isup / chanspec / dfs_status every 15 s, rchqd reads
chanim_stats every 10 s. restart_wireless() has stopped the first two since
v3.2.8, but the net / allnet / net_and_phy / wps_enr branches tear the
radios down without that and never drop wlready, so rpunctd's own guard
was blind. Owner RT-BE96U, 2026-10-13 and 2026-10-14: a GUI IPv6 change ran
restart_net and seven seconds into the teardown both Dynamic radios'
firmware trapped (dhdpcie_checkdied, TRAP type 0x4 @ 0x80f084 on wl1 and
wl2 alike); they answered "wl driver adapter not found" until a power
cycle while every client sat on 2.4 GHz. wl0, which no reader touched,
survived both times. reaper_wl_readers_stop() (the three stops, then a
wait of REAPER_WL_WINDOW_MS + 600 ms when rpunctd was running, so an armed
window closes before the teardown) and reaper_wl_readers_start() are
called beside stop_acsd() / start_acsd() - the stock daemon of the same
class, which stock already sequences - in every teardown branch and in
restart_wireless(). shared/reaper_wlquiet.c: reaper_wl_tearing_down()
(rc_service names a radio-stopping service, whole tokens) and
reaper_wl_quiet() (that, or wlready != 1) are the readers' own check,
keyed by rpunctd's radio_quiet(), bwfloor's tick and rchqd's tick. Metal:
two restart_net on the owner box with Dynamic on, radios up, no trap, the
new rpunctd paused on rc_service until the branch finished. Lean:
tests/test_wl_readers_quiesce.py (the predicate host-compiled and run).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
